[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573875270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101168#issuecomment-2573875270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101168","id":2573875270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZajhG","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T20:31:40Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T20:31:40Z","body":"I just tried it and it looks fine (and useful), however selecting a node with its own special handles it will still cause these handles to show up - e.g. selecting a CollisionShape3D shows the handles to resize the shape, so you can still accidentally change something you didn't mean to:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a52d3483-d411-4ca8-b95f-1eadc8f47f80)\r\n\r\nShouldn't these handles also not show up when in selection-only mode?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573875270/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573917294","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101168#issuecomment-2573917294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101168","id":2573917294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zatxu","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T21:00:08Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T21:00:08Z","body":">Shouldn't these handles also not show up when in selection-only mode?\r\n\r\nI thought for a bit on this when developing this functionality and decided against it because I figured if you're selecting a collision node for example, you are trying to actively modify it (but not necessarily its transform). Typically, those gizmos are not occluding anything behind them that you would want to select, at least not as bad as the transform gizmo. In Blender for example you also have a few special gimzos you can modify even in select mode. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573917294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573941472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101168#issuecomment-2573941472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101168","id":2573941472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zazrg","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T21:16:29Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T21:16:29Z","body":"Yeah i guess this might be a bit niche (i do not have strong opinion either way) and if needed it could most likely be done as a separate \"View ...\" check in the viewport menu alongside \"View gizmos\", \"View transform gizmo\", etc.\r\n\r\nActually, is the \"View transform gizmo\" option even needed anymore with this PR?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573941472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573953706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101168#issuecomment-2573953706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101168","id":2573953706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Za2qq","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T21:25:17Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T21:28:20Z","body":">Actually, is the \"View transform gizmo\" option even needed anymore with this PR?\r\n\r\nI personally like it because it allows you to do certain things that maybe you can't with other modes/settings. For example, hiding the transform gizmo only applies to single viewport. Also, the underlying function of the chosen mode still works even without the gizmo being visible, like being able to rotate an object by just dragging anywhere on the screen. Of course, using blender instant transform bindings can serve a similar purpose, but some people might prefer the alternative this functionality offers.\r\n\r\nIn general, I'm of the philosophy that you should be able to hide or modify just about everything. I made a proposal a while back to change the editor viewport message to a label so even that can be hidden/modified at least via plugins: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8789 \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2c91b0e-9071-4d5e-a5f8-abce92a04b01\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573953706/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573973435","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101168#issuecomment-2573973435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101168","id":2573973435,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Za7e7","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T21:38:54Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T21:39:42Z","body":"> Also, the underlying function of the chosen mode still works even without the gizmo being visible, like being able to rotate an object by just dragging anywhere on the screen.\r\n\r\nAh yeah you are correct. This is very useful for 2D views (i mean the axis aligned orthographic views in 3D scene) though Godot's implementation is a bit lacking because you can't change the selected item from any mode, it doesn't work in the multi-gizmo mode and in 3D it is pretty much never what you want (it should really only be used for translation even in multi-gizmo mode and use the closest plane box instead of a screen aligned plane).\r\n\r\nI first encountered something similar in Radiant (the level editor family) and while it took me a long time to get used to it, i realized it can be *much* faster to work with than the more common \"point and click on a handle/arrow/widget to move it\" approach most tools use.\r\n\r\nThat'd probably be something for a new proposal though, not really relevant to this PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573973435/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2725032797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101168#issuecomment-2725032797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101168","id":2725032797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ibLNd","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://av